@startuml SD_Add_To_Cart
!theme cerulean-outline

title Add to Cart Flow (Client-Side Only)\nAdventureWorks Sales BI Platform

actor       "User"               as User
participant "Browser / React\n(ProductDetails Page)" as React     #LightBlue
participant "CartContext\n(React Context)"            as CartCtx   #LightCyan
participant "localStorage\n(ecom_cart_v1)"            as Storage   #LightYellow
participant "Navbar\n(Cart Badge)"                    as Navbar    #LightGreen

note over React, Storage
  The cart is entirely client-side.
  No API calls are made when adding items to cart.
  Cart state lives in React Context + localStorage.
end note

== User Views Product ==

User -> React : Viewing ProductDetails page\nProduct: { id, name, price, stockQty, ... }
React --> User : Shows product info,\nquantity selector,\n"Add to Cart" button

== Add to Cart ==

User -> React : Sets quantity (e.g. qty = 2)\nClicks **"Add to Cart"**

React -> CartCtx : cart.add(product, qty)

CartCtx -> CartCtx : const q = Math.max(1, qty)

alt Product already in cart
    CartCtx -> CartCtx : Find existing CartItem\nwhere item.product.id === product.id
    CartCtx -> CartCtx : Update qty:\nMath.min(\n  existingQty + q,\n  product.stockQty\n)
    note right of CartCtx : Caps at stockQty\nto prevent over-ordering
else Product not in cart
    CartCtx -> CartCtx : Push new CartItem:\n{ product, qty: Math.min(q, stockQty) }
end

CartCtx -> CartCtx : setItems(updatedItems)\nTriggers React re-render

== Persist to localStorage ==

CartCtx -> CartCtx : useEffect detects\nitems state change

CartCtx -> Storage : localStorage.setItem(\n  "ecom_cart_v1",\n  JSON.stringify(items)\n)

note right of Storage
  Stored as JSON array:
  [
    {
      "product": { id, name, price, ... },
      "qty": 2
    }
  ]
end note

== UI Updates (via React Context) ==

CartCtx -> CartCtx : Recompute derived state:\n  count = items.reduce(sum + qty)\n  total = items.reduce(sum + qty * price)

CartCtx -> Navbar : Context re-render propagates\nto all CartContext consumers
Navbar -> Navbar : Update cart badge\ncount = {cart.count}
Navbar --> User : Badge shows updated\nitem count (e.g. "2")

CartCtx -> React : Re-render ProductDetails\nif cart state referenced
React --> User : Visual feedback:\n"Added to cart" confirmation

== Cart Restoration on Page Reload ==

note over CartCtx, Storage
  On app startup (CartProvider mount):
end note

User -> React : Refreshes page / reopens app
React -> CartCtx : CartProvider initializes
CartCtx -> Storage : localStorage.getItem("ecom_cart_v1")
Storage --> CartCtx : JSON string
CartCtx -> CartCtx : JSON.parse(raw)\nFilter valid items:\n  x.product exists\n  x.product.id is number
CartCtx -> CartCtx : useState initialized\nwith restored items
CartCtx -> Navbar : Badge shows persisted count
Navbar --> User : Cart badge reflects\nprevious session items

@enduml
